# Rejox frontend — environment configuration.
# Copy to .env for local development. Never commit .env.

# Base URL of the Rejox backend. **Leave this empty for local development.**
#
# Empty means same-origin: the app calls `/api` on the origin it is served from
# and the Vite dev server proxies that to the backend (see vite.config.ts).
# Production has the same shape behind a reverse proxy.
#
# That is not a style choice — it is the only shape in which signing in works.
# The session cookie is `SameSite=Lax`, so the browser will not send it to a
# different origin. Point this at `http://localhost:8000` while the app runs on
# `:5173` and sign-in appears to succeed and then silently never sticks: every
# request after it arrives with no cookie.
#
# Set it only for a client that authenticates with an API KEY instead of a
# cookie — a script, or the app served from somewhere the API is not proxied.
VITE_API_URL=
